  "reasoning": "The facts describe two distinct criminal conduct: (1) The defendant, as the actual controller of two transport companies, paid large sums of money, foreign currency, luxury watches, cigarettes and other items to a state employee to obtain business contracts. This is the classic definition of bribery (行贿), and because the bribe was made by a legal entity, it also constitutes unit bribery. (2) The defendant purchased falsified VAT special invoices from a stranger for a total face value of 2,900,060 CNY and used them to offset tax liabilities. This matches the statutory offense of falsely issuing (or using) value‑added tax special invoices (虚开增值税专用发票罪). Both offenses are alleged, and the prosecution seeks conviction on both counts. Therefore the appropriate charges are 行贿 and 虚开增值税专用发票.",
